# Testing (Kinsenas)

This rule is the **single source of truth** for how Kinsenas writes and runs tests. It supersedes conflicting test guidance elsewhere in cursor rules or user instructions.

Related: [feature-planning.mdc](./feature-planning.mdc), [plan-implementation.mdc](./plan-implementation.mdc), [feature-plans.mdc](./feature-plans.mdc).

## Workflow (standard order)

Every behavior change follows this sequence:

1. **Impact analysis** — complete the checklist in [feature-planning.mdc](./feature-planning.mdc); list affected files, flows, seeders, and **existing tests**.
2. **Conflict resolution** — if behaviors, scope, tests, or rules conflict, **stop and ask the user** what to retain vs remove (see below). Record decisions in the plan before writing tests or code.
3. **RED** — write **failing** tests first (Unit → Feature → Browser as applicable).
4. **GREEN** — implement the minimum code until new tests pass.
5. **REFACTOR** — clean up with tests still green.
6. **Regression** — update or fix tests listed in the impact matrix.
7. **Scoped tests green** — run all tests **in scope for the current task** before marking plan work complete (see [Running tests](#running-tests)).

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Impact analysis] --> B{Conflicts?}
    B -->|Yes| C[Ask retain / remove]
    C --> D[Record decisions in plan]
    D --> E[RED — failing tests]
    B -->|No| E
    E --> F[GREEN — implement]
    F --> G[REFACTOR]
    G --> H[Fix regression tests]
    H --> I[Scoped tests green]
```

## Conflict resolution

When impact analysis or implementation reveals **conflicting behavior, scope, tests, or rules**, do **not** resolve automatically.

1. **Stop** — do not delete routes, UI, enums, or tests until the user decides.
2. **Ask** the user feature-wise what to **retain** and what to **remove**.
3. Present each conflict as a decision card:

| Field | Content |
| ----- | ------- |
| **Context** | What changed and what it touches |
| **Current behavior** | What exists today |
| **Proposed behavior** | What the plan wants |
| **Affected surfaces** | Routes, pages, tests, mobile, seeders |
| **Options** | **Retain** / **Replace** / **Hybrid** / **Defer** |
| **Recommendation** | Agent suggestion and why |

4. **Record** the user's choice in the plan `## Decisions` section and in the breakdown `## Decisions` table.
5. **Align** the impact matrix, test todos, and implementation to the recorded decision.
6. Use structured questions (`AskQuestion`) when there are 2–4 concrete options.

**Ask when:** deprecating behavior, tests disagree on expectations, mobile vs web diverge, seed/demo data assumes an old model, or two features cannot both stay.

**Skip asking when:** single obvious bug fix, pure rename/refactor with unchanged behavior, or copy/CSS-only with impact matrix marked N/A.

## Test pyramid

| Layer | Directory | Use for |
| ----- | --------- | ------- |
| **Unit** | `tests/Unit/` | Pure service logic, calculators, formatters — no HTTP |
| **Feature** | `tests/Feature/` | Routes, validation, policies, API JSON, Inertia props |
| **Browser** | `tests/Browser/` | User-visible flows, modals, navigation, JS errors — [Pest browser testing](https://pestphp.com/docs/browser-testing) |

**Do not add Laravel Dusk.** Use `pestphp/pest-plugin-browser` (Playwright) only.

### When each layer is required

| Change type | Unit | Feature | Browser |
| ----------- | ---- | ------- | ------- |
| New/changed service logic | Required if isolatable | If exposed via HTTP | N/A |
| New API endpoint | Optional | Required | N/A |
| New/changed Inertia page or workflow | N/A | Props/redirects | Required (smoke or happy path) |
| Modal / confirmation UX | N/A | Optional | Required |
| Auth / vault flow | N/A | Required | Extend browser pattern |
| Copy / CSS only, no behavior | N/A | N/A | N/A — document N/A in impact matrix |

## TDD rules

- **Tests before implementation** for behavior changes — write failing tests in the same pass before production code (RED first).
- **Do not** implement ambiguous behavior when the impact matrix shows conflicts — resolve with the user first.
- Use **Arrange–Act–Assert** in every test; meaningful factory data (e.g. `'email' => 'admin@kinsenas.test'`).
- Use `php artisan make:test --pest {name}`; pass `--unit` for unit tests.
- All tests use **Pest** — never PHPUnit class syntax.
- Do **not** remove test files without user approval.

### Running tests

**In scope** for a task means:

- New tests written for this change (Unit, Feature, Browser as applicable)
- Existing tests listed in the impact matrix (regression)
- Any sibling test files that share setup or behavior you touched (e.g. same controller, page, or service)

Do **not** run the full suite during TDD unless the user explicitly asks. Run only what is in scope.

| When | What to run |
| ---- | ----------- |
| During RED/GREEN cycles | The test file or `--filter=` for the test being written |
| Before marking plan work complete | **All in-scope tests** — new + impact-matrix regression files (one command per file or directory, or `--filter=` when grouped) |
| User asks for full suite | `php artisan test --compact` |
| In breakdowns / handoff | List **suggested** in-scope commands (Feature + Browser paths) |
| User explicitly asks not to run | Skip execution; still write tests and list suggested commands |

Use `php artisan test --compact tests/Feature/ExampleTest.php` for a single file.

**CI** runs `composer ci:check` (full Pest suite + Playwright) on pull requests — that is the full-suite gate, not local TDD.

## Browser testing (Pest + Playwright)

Stack is already installed: `pestphp/pest-plugin-browser`, Playwright in CI (`.github/workflows/tests.yml`).

### Conventions

- Tests live in `tests/Browser/`.
- Use `visit('/')` and Pest browser API (`click`, `fill`, `assertSee`, etc.).
- Prefer **`data-test` selectors** via `@name` (e.g. `click('@login-button')`) — add `data-test` to new interactive UI when missing.
- Call `assertNoSmoke()` on smoke tests (no console logs / JS errors).
- Use `visit('/')->on()->mobile()` or `iPhone14Pro()` for mobile-relevant flows.
- Screenshots go to `tests/Browser/Screenshots/` (gitignored).
- Reuse Laravel test helpers: `RefreshDatabase`, factories, seeders in `beforeEach` (match sibling Feature tests).
- For authenticated savings flows, plan browser helpers (login → vault unlock → seeded plan) — mirror `tests/Pest.php` Feature helpers.

### Example pattern

See `tests/Browser/LoginTest.php` and `tests/Browser/WelcomeTest.php`.

### Debug

- `php artisan test --compact tests/Browser/LoginTest.php --debug` for headed pause on failure
- Docs: https://pestphp.com/docs/browser-testing

## Kinsenas test helpers

Reuse existing patterns:

- `Tests\Concerns\UnlocksVault` — encrypted savings tests
- `tests/Pest.php` — `grantTeamSubscriptionAccess()`, `createUserWithPlan()`, `fakeGhlApi()`, etc.
- Seed in `beforeEach`: `BillingSeeder`, `SavingsFormulaTemplateSeeder` where sibling Feature tests do

## Plan and breakdown requirements

Plans ([feature-plans.mdc](./feature-plans.mdc)) must include todos in this order when behavior changes:

1. `impact-analysis`
2. `resolve-conflicts` (if any — otherwise skip)
3. `failing-unit-tests` / `failing-feature-tests` / `failing-browser-tests` (as applicable)
4. `implement`
5. `update-regression-tests`
6. `scoped-tests-green`

Plans must include a `## Decisions` section when conflicts were resolved.

Breakdowns ([plan-implementation.mdc](./plan-implementation.mdc)) must include:

- **Decisions** table (when applicable)
- **Suggested tests** with Feature and Browser paths
- **Visual QA** for Inertia/UI changes

## Exceptions

Document in the impact matrix as **N/A** with one-line rationale:

- Copy or styling with no behavior change
- Cursor rules or agent config only
- Dependency bumps with no app logic change

Even for exceptions, run in-scope tests when behavior could regress in touched areas; rely on CI for the full suite.
